      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/0ca6c9e91c17cea351f60cc475f0feab876a29a4877114c06ce9408863a8f7dc.png)\n\nPart of the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ with period $2$ is shown above. What is the graph of $y=f(x)$ on the interval $-4\\le x\\le 4?$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph above shows the function in the interval $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nSince this interval has length $2,$ and the period of the function is also $2,$ this interval represents a single period of the function.\n\nTherefore, the function will consist of many copies of the shape shown above, shifted horizontally by multiples of $2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/cc628e23b36aa95aa47e42c6bae14caf29651c46abcea1bf26408b44f2660f10.png)",
